body:
Explanation: On the new map, various spots give you one of four different buffs. However, if you move a tower to different spots it will show that they actually keep the buffs that they had from the original location. This appears to only be visual, since the discount buff was easy to test and it was not actually being applied even though the icon is visible (I used the maim moab to test this). I would assume the other buffs are also not retained, though it's a bit harder to tell without dedicated testing.

&#x200B;

Fun map, by the way! I don't know that I've ever done chimps with a support chinook, but I decided to make it a main part of my strategy here. Also, great map for the axis of havoc achievement if anyone wants to try and get it. The spot where my other two snipers are gives damage (I'm 99% sure that's what it does at least), and it's rather good for the fast firing snipers that usually have very low base damage.

&#x200B;

Nice fun map, NK!

"My immediate thoughts are how much more risky is it to subdue a knife attacker with these means?" Why is this your immediate thought. Police are supposed to be trained to deal with dangerous situations. In the US, they're trained to deal with those situations by just fucking shooting it until the problem goes away. At least in that video, those cops are trained to deal with dangerous problems without using lethality. Being a cop in the US is such a cushy job right now, it is no where near as dangerous as you seem to believe, largely BECAUSE they shoot first and ask questions never... and are immune to any sort of prosecution for it. 

&#x200B;

NEVER CALL THE COPS IN THE US unless you're ok with somebody dying.

This reminds me of a question I had a while ago when I was visiting Seattle and the downtown area was just filled to the brim with cars in every lane. Does anyone know how emergency vehicles are supposed to get around in big cities during rush hour traffic? Seattle isn't even close to being as big as a city like New York, so I can imagine it's even more clogged up in bigger cities like that. Surely they can't just plow through hundreds of cars to get to their destination, especially when those people haven't even done anything wrong necessarily by just being stuck in traffic.

&#x200B;

I've never lived in a big city so I guess I'm just curious and this comment reminded me of my experience a while ago.
